# Image Handling Rules

## Read-only source image is immutable

The project contains a read-only source/reference image and one or more writable
test images used for kernel development and testing.

The read-only source/reference image is strictly immutable.

NEVER:

- delete files or directories from the read-only source/reference image;
- modify files inside the read-only source/reference image;
- overwrite, recreate, truncate, or otherwise alter the read-only source/reference image;
- use the read-only source/reference image as a writable workspace;
- mount or manipulate the read-only source/reference image in a way that can
  modify its contents.

Preserve the read-only source/reference image exactly as provided.

## Writable test images

Kernel development, testing, packaging, and temporary cleanup may be performed
on writable test images.

When additional free space is required in a writable test image for the kernel,
the following paths are explicitly authorized for deletion:

- `/docpack`
- `/develop/fasm`
- `/3d/view3ds`
- `/games/dino`

These paths may be deleted only from the writable test image currently being
used for kernel testing.

Their deletion is intentional and authorized by the user.

## Deletion restrictions

The authorization above is limited to exactly these three paths:

- `/docpack`
- `/develop/fasm`
- `/3d/view3ds`
- `/games/dino`

Do NOT delete any other files or directories from a test image unless the user
explicitly authorizes them.

Do NOT interpret the authorization as permission to recursively clean arbitrary
unused files.

Do NOT delete any of the approved paths from the read-only source/reference
image.

## Before deleting anything

Before performing a deletion, determine which image is being modified.

The agent MUST verify that:

1. the target is the writable test image;
2. the target is not the read-only source/reference image;
3. the path being deleted is one of the explicitly authorized paths above.

If there is any uncertainty about which image is mounted or being modified,
STOP and ask the user before deleting anything.

## Purpose

The purpose of deleting the approved paths is to reclaim space in writable test
images so that the kernel and its test artifacts can be built, packaged, and
tested.

This rule does not authorize any changes to the project's source tree merely to
free image space.

## Priority

These rules apply to all Cursor Agent work in this repository and should be
followed in every session.

If a future user instruction explicitly changes or supersedes these rules, follow
the newer explicit instruction, while continuing to protect the read-only
source/reference image unless the user explicitly authorizes modification of it.